    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Fix it Yourself: Maya's Rainbow Page\r\n\r\n*\"I asked for a colorful page but it looks like a rainbow exploded! Every single thing is a different color. That's not what I meant at all. I wanted it to feel fun and bright, not chaotic.\"*\r\n\r\nSo far, AI has made every change for you. This time **you** are the one editing the code - AI Tutor can explain things, but it won't write code on this level.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. **Read:** Open `index.html` and find the `<style>` block at the top. Each rule sets a `color` or `background-color` for one kind of element.\r\n2. **Edit:** Change the color values yourself. Pick 2-3 colors that look good together. Color names like `navy`, `white`, or `gold` work - so do hex codes like `#336699`.\r\n3. **Check:** Watch the preview update as you edit. Keep tweaking until the page feels fun and bright - not chaotic.\r\n\r\n> **Hint:** Stuck on what a rule does? Ask AI Tutor to *explain* it - just remember, on this level the typing is all yours.\r\n\r\nWhen Maya's page looks fun instead of chaotic, click **Continue**.",
